pack habitat-human-factors-work
generation control-1
source_plane run2_relationship_adoption
item_kind habitat_human_factors
source_ref campaign:habitat-human-factors
note Sequenced deliberately: the UTA path can produce real criticism and introductions first, which is what gives the cold outreach something behind it. Priorities encode that order. Nothing is sent until the identity-verification item clears.

work hhf_verify_all_identities
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 9.5
  reason Every actor in this pack is asserted from an unverified brief. Confirm names, titles, departments and current affiliation from each institution's own directory. A wrong title in a cold academic email is disqualifying, and Mel Sellick's non-IEEE affiliation is not recorded at all

work hhf_define_narrow_question_per_scholar
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 9.0
  reason Each person gets one aspect to criticize, not a product tour. Epley on whether mediated presence increases or substitutes for human connection; Mark on interruption cost; Hancock on AI-mediated communication asymmetry; Schroeder on felt-understanding across modality; Waytz on over-attribution to spatialized agents; Sellick on organizational relational readiness

work hhf_contact_wetz
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 8.5
  reason First contact. Former EE/PPEL student returning for research criticism, asking for perspective and introductions rather than endorsement. As Associate Chair he is positioned to route to the right people

work hhf_contact_tjuatja
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 7.0
  reason Second existing EE relationship, same framing. Only if there was genuine personal contact -- otherwise this is a cold email wearing a warm one's clothes

work hhf_contact_sellick
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 8.0
  reason Closest single match: UTA already hosted her on exactly this question and P7023 overlaps organizational Habitat design. Needs her current affiliation resolved first

work hhf_contact_uta_hci
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 7.5
  reason Torres, Gieser and Makedon can criticize the spatial interaction itself. Gieser is the closest on VR/XR and human-robot interaction

work hhf_contact_uta_io_psych
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 6.5
  reason Kenworthy and Watts for workplace measurement and design. The I-O lens is what turns opinions into instruments

work hhf_external_scholar_outreach
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 5.0
  reason Epley, Mark, Hancock, Schroeder, Waytz. Deliberately last: cold outreach lands far better carrying prior criticism and a real measurement plan. Schroeder co-authors with Epley, so one warm path may serve two

work hhf_pilot_protocol_three_conditions
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 8.0
  reason Build the A/B/C protocol -- conventional surface, Habitat spatial state, Habitat plus resident social agents -- over one realistic multi-stage work episode. Feasible without IRB for early design criticism, and gives every scholar something concrete to attack

work hhf_instrument_selection
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason Choose validated instruments rather than inventing scales. Cognitive load, loneliness, belonging, trust calibration and affect all have established measures; using homemade ones would make any result unciteable

work hhf_human_connection_preservation_principle
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.5
  reason Encode the named principle: AI-mediated social presence must not silently substitute for human connection where human connection is materially valuable. ProviderGraph would need to distinguish answer-a-factual-question from resolve-an-ambiguous-conflict-with-a-coworker

work hhf_attention_budget_observables
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.5
  reason Model an attention budget from observables only -- context transitions, interruption counts, room reheats, AI-initiated versus human-initiated contacts. Never infer emotional state. "19 context transitions in 22 minutes" is defensible; "Nick seems stressed" is not

work hhf_cooling_gets_cognitive_axis
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.0
  reason Structural cooling currently means computational quiet. It should also mean visual, social and cognitive quiet: a cooled item must not glow, pulse, move or hold central spatial attention either. Same reheat condition governs all four

work hhf_habitat_thesis_writeup
  target_plane run3_four_economies_campaign
  priority 5.5
  reason Habitat's stated reason to exist becomes a research thesis rather than a UI theme. That framing is also what makes it legible to Tarbell and to ACM
